    "background_story": "Ramon was a gentle soul with a passion for the outdoors. Growing up in the Kentish countryside, he spent most of his childhood exploring the woods and meadows. One autumn, while wandering through the woods, Ramon stumbled upon a hidden copse of hazel trees laden with cobnuts. Enchanted by the rustic charm of the wild nuts, he began to tend to the trees, learning the art of sustainable foraging from his grandfather. As the years passed, Ramon became known throughout the region for his exceptional cobnuts, carefully hand-picked and sold at local markets. His love for the land and the simple pleasures of life earned him the nickname 'The Cobnut Man'. Ramon's dedication to preserving traditional farming practices inspired a new generation of environmentalists and food enthusiasts.",
